The cable example contains an adaptation patch derived from Newton.
Its upstream notices and license are retained in
examples/cable_calibration/solver/NEWTON-LICENSE.md.
Source revisions and hashes are recorded alongside the patch.

Archived cable observations, outputs and reports retain their provenance.
Historical experimental results are not new validation results for this seed.

The optional SolverMuJoCo integration uses MuJoCo and MuJoCo Warp,
both licensed under Apache-2.0. These separately installed dependencies
retain their own license files and third-party notices.

The optional robot import example uses trimesh (MIT), Pillow (MIT-CMU),
and SciPy (BSD-3-Clause).
These separately installed dependencies retain their own license files and
third-party notices. The bundled two-link model and mesh are project fixtures.

The optional UR5e integration check downloads a pinned model from MuJoCo Menagerie
(google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie), licensed under BSD-3-Clause. Its original
license is retained in the downloaded source and exported resource bundle.

Project documentation is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International; see LICENSE-DOCS. Bundled software example fixtures, including
archived observations, outputs, reports, and solver adaptations, retain their
Apache-2.0 terms.

The optional Go2 sysid downloader retrieves the Unitree Go2 model from
google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie and measurements from
iit-DLSLab/sim2real-robot-identification at the revisions in
examples/actuator/robot/go2/sources.json. Both sources provide BSD-3-Clause
licenses, retained with the downloads. The model, meshes and measurements
are not distributed with this repository.
